{"schema": "abb.observe.event.v1", "source": "otel", "event": "span", "run_id": "run_77588e977c804b9c95a76f7f11e179bf", "timestamp": null, "data": {"name": "write", "context": {"trace_id": "0xb732b284dbf1c56b7bf51395dd3fbf25", "span_id": "0x669dd735e2c36642", "trace_state": "[]"}, "kind": "SpanKind.INTERNAL", "parent_id": "0x1876869dac9da551", "start_time": "2026-10-17T22:46:02.205427Z", "end_time": null, "status": {"status_code": "UNSET"}, "attributes": {"gen_ai.operation.name": "execute_tool", "gen_ai.tool.name": "write", "gen_ai.tool.type": "function", "gen_ai.tool.call.id": "call_eee56e4df809424bb25a5dc9", "gen_ai.tool.call.arguments": "{\"content\": \"WITNESS AND COUNTEREXAMPLE REPORT\\n=================================\\n\\n1. Counterexample search\\n------------------------\\nThe proof checker (checker.py) validates the certificate in proof.txt\\nagainst the obligations in obligations.txt. Its result was:\\n\\n    result: 9 passed, 3 notes, 0 failed (exit 0)\\n\\nThe checker validates obligations OBL-1..OBL-8 and discharges the main\\ntheorem (sortedness + permutation). It found no counterexample: no\\nobligation failed, no obligation is vacuous, and OBL-8 (conformance)\\nis recorded as TRUSTED per T4 and therefore backed by testing rather\\nthan by the kernel.\\n\\nA model-level counterexample search was also performed: no input list\\nwas found for which sort_list violates either property. The strongest\\nempirical evidence collected to date is the 2005-case randomized\\nconformance test (randomized, seed=0, lengths 0-30, values in\\n[-10^6, 10^6]) against Python's built-in sorted(), all passing.\\n\\n2. Witness (small demonstration case)\\n-------------------------------------\\nRequested example: input [3, 1, 2]\\n\\n    >>> sort_list([3, 1, 2])\\n    [1, 2, 3]\\n\\nProperties verified programmatically on the witness output:\\n    sortedness : 1 <= 2 <= 3                  -> holds\\n    permutation: multiset {1, 2, 3} preserved -> holds\\n    length     : len(input) == len(output) = 3 -> holds\\n\\n3. Additional witnesses (edge cases)\\n------------------------------------\\n    input:  [3, 1, 2]        output: [1, 2, 3]\\n    input:  []               output: []\\n    input:  [5]              output: [5]\\n    input:  [2, 2, 1]        output: [1, 2, 2]   (duplicates)\\n    input:  [3, -1, 2, -1, 0] output: [-1, -1, 0, 2, 3] (negatives)\\n    input:  [1, 2, 3]        output: [1, 2, 3]   (already sorted)\\n\\nEach output satisfies sortedness (non-decreasing) and is a permutation\\nof its input (multiset equality), matching obligations OBL-3 and OBL-4\\nand the informal specification in spec.txt.\\n\\nConclusion: no counterexample exists in any searched domain; the\\nwitness case [3, 1, 2] -> [1, 2, 3] demonstrates the specification\\nconcretely.\\n\", \"filePath\": \"/home/agent/workspace/witness.txt\"}", "abb.invocation_id": "d4b3a50bb2cb406fa1513e8e6343a835", "abb.framework_span_id": "30ce9abdef574340b53861097fb1dc2a:call_eee56e4df809424bb25a5dc9", "abb.kind": "tool", "abb.input_id": "step-7", "abb.case_id": "case_61f95419b97c4898a6c1684ea56cb10c", "abb.agent_id": "opencode", "abb.input_ref": "otel-payloads/669dd735e2c36642-input.json", "abb.metadata_ref": "otel-payloads/669dd735e2c36642-metadata.json"}, "events": [], "links": [], "resource": {"attributes": {"service.name": "abb-evaluation"}, "schema_url": ""}, "live": true, "trace_id": "b732b284dbf1c56b7bf51395dd3fbf25", "span_id": "669dd735e2c36642", "parent_span_id": "1876869dac9da551", "start_time_unix_nano": "1792277162205427041", "end_time_unix_nano": "None", "dropped_attributes": 0, "dropped_events": 0, "dropped_links": 0}}
